{{define "main"}}
<!-- Hero Section -->
<section class="page-hero" id="operational-assessment-hero">
    <div class="hero-content--centered">
        <div class="hero-kicker">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-size-sm">analytics</span>
            <span class="eyebrow">TAMS-Powered Cybersecurity Maturity Assessment</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="hero-title">
            Know Your Cybersecurity Maturity. <span>Know What Comes Next.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="hero-description">
            Give executives, security leaders, and compliance teams a shared view of what is working, where risk is accumulating, and which improvements deserve attention first. Tabiri Analytics Management System (TAMS) adapts to your responses across six essential cybersecurity domains instead of forcing your organization through a generic checklist.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="btn-primary" href="/contact">Schedule an Operational Assessment</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Customer Triggers -->
<section class="content-section content-section--light content-section--border-bottom" id="when-to-assess">
    <div class="section-container">
        <div class="section-intro">
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent">When to Assess</p>
            <h2 class="section-heading">Replace Assumptions with a <span>Defensible Baseline</span></h2>
            <p class="section-intro__description">Assess when leadership needs more than a policy inventory: a current view of how security decisions and controls work across the organization.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-grid">
            <article class="trust-card group">
                <div class="card-heading-row"><div class="icon-tile icon-tile--primary"><span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-tile__symbol">gavel</span></div><h3 class="heading-medium"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Meet Scrutiny</span></h3></div>
                <p class="body-copy-small">Prepare for regulatory review, customer due diligence, cyber insurance renewal, board reporting, or a formal compliance initiative with evidence your stakeholders can use.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="trust-card group">
                <div class="card-heading-row"><div class="icon-tile icon-tile--primary"><span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-tile__symbol">sync_alt</span></div><h3 class="heading-medium"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Navigate Change</span></h3></div>
                <p class="body-copy-small">Reassess after rapid growth, leadership changes, an acquisition, cloud migration, new critical systems, or an incident changes your operating assumptions.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="trust-card group">
                <div class="card-heading-row"><div class="icon-tile icon-tile--primary"><span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-tile__symbol">target</span></div><h3 class="heading-medium"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Direct Investment</span></h3></div>
                <p class="body-copy-small">Give decision-makers a consistent basis for prioritizing budget, ownership, and remediation instead of allowing the loudest concern to set the security agenda.</p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- TAMS Workflow -->
<section class="content-section content-section--muted content-section--border-bottom" id="tams-workflow">
    <div class="section-container">
        <div class="section-intro">
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent">The TAMS Experience</p>
            <h2 class="section-heading">A Structured Assessment That <span>Adapts to Your Answers</span></h2>
            <p class="section-intro__description">Authorized respondents sign in to TAMS, complete the assessment online, and receive a maturity view generated from their responses.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-grid">
            <article class="trust-card group">
                <div class="card-heading-row">
                    <div class="icon-tile icon-tile--primary"><span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-tile__symbol">passkey</span></div>
                    <h3 class="heading-medium"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Secure Access</span></h3>
                </div>
                <p class="body-copy-small">Each respondent receives login access to complete the assessment through the TAMS online workspace.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="trust-card group">
                <div class="card-heading-row">
                    <div class="icon-tile icon-tile--primary"><span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-tile__symbol">account_tree</span></div>
                    <h3 class="heading-medium"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Adaptive Questions</span></h3>
                </div>
                <p class="body-copy-small">TAMS uses each response to present relevant follow-up questions, capturing context beyond a fixed checklist.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="trust-card group">
                <div class="card-heading-row">
                    <div class="icon-tile icon-tile--primary"><span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-tile__symbol">neurology</span></div>
                    <h3 class="heading-medium"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Agentic AI Scoring</span></h3>
                </div>
                <p class="body-copy-small">The application evaluates completed responses automatically to produce a consistent view of cybersecurity maturity.</p>
            </article>
        </div>
        <div class="proof-card proof-card--spaced">
            <div class="method-note__content">
                <span class="material-symbols-outlined">account_tree</span>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="heading-medium heading-medium--compact"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Depth Where Your Answers Require It</span></h3>
                    <p class="body-copy body-copy--relaxed">A static questionnaire asks every organization the same questions and leaves analysts to reconstruct context later. TAMS follows relevant response paths while the assessment is underway, capturing ownership, scope, frequency, implementation, and supporting technology where those details affect the maturity view.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Assessment Domains -->
<section class="content-section content-section--light" id="assessment-domains">
    <div class="section-container">
        <div class="section-intro">
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent">Six Operational Domains</p>
            <h2 class="section-heading">See Maturity Across the <span>Whole Security Program</span></h2>
            <p class="section-intro__description">The questionnaire moves from leadership and risk decisions through technical safeguards and incident operations.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-grid feature-grid--two-to-three">
            <article class="trust-card group">
                <div class="card-heading-row"><div class="icon-tile icon-tile--primary"><span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-tile__symbol">corporate_fare</span></div><h3 class="heading-medium"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Security Governance</span></h3></div>
                <p class="body-copy-small">Examine oversight, policies, roles, awareness, and the processes used to sustain the security program.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="trust-card group">
                <div class="card-heading-row"><div class="icon-tile icon-tile--primary"><span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-tile__symbol">warning</span></div><h3 class="heading-medium"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Security Risk Management</span></h3></div>
                <p class="body-copy-small">Assess how cyber risks are identified, evaluated, treated, tracked, and communicated across the organization.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="trust-card group">
                <div class="card-heading-row"><div class="icon-tile icon-tile--primary"><span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-tile__symbol">shield_lock</span></div><h3 class="heading-medium"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Data Protection</span></h3></div>
                <p class="body-copy-small">Review the safeguards and operating practices used to manage and protect sensitive information.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="trust-card group">
                <div class="card-heading-row"><div class="icon-tile icon-tile--primary"><span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-tile__symbol">manage_accounts</span></div><h3 class="heading-medium"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Access Management</span></h3></div>
                <p class="body-copy-small">Evaluate how identities, privileges, authentication, and access lifecycles are governed and controlled.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="trust-card group">
                <div class="card-heading-row"><div class="icon-tile icon-tile--primary"><span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-tile__symbol">architecture</span></div><h3 class="heading-medium"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Security Architecture</span></h3></div>
                <p class="body-copy-small">Measure operational controls across infrastructure, endpoints, applications, monitoring, and protective technologies.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="trust-card group">
                <div class="card-heading-row"><div class="icon-tile icon-tile--primary"><span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-tile__symbol">emergency</span></div><h3 class="heading-medium"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Incident Response</span></h3></div>
                <p class="body-copy-small">Assess readiness, detection, containment, investigation, remediation, and the use of incident metrics.</p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Assessment Method -->
<section class="content-section content-section--muted content-section--bordered" id="assessment-method">
    <div class="method-layout">
        <div>
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent">From Response to Insight</p>
            <h2 class="section-heading">More Context Than a <span>One-Size-Fits-All Checklist</span></h2>
            <p class="body-copy method-intro">The assessment combines structured choices with contextual follow-ups. Depending on the topic and response, TAMS can ask about frequency, scope, ownership, process detail, supporting technology, or the extent of implementation.</p>
            <div class="method-note method-note--white">
                <div class="method-note__content">
                    <span class="material-symbols-outlined">fact_check</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="heading-medium heading-medium--compact"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Built Around Real Operations</span></h3>
                        <p class="body-copy-small-compact">Questions cover both documented controls and how those controls are implemented, reviewed, managed, and measured in practice.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <ol class="process-steps">
            <li class="trust-card-no-hover process-step-card"><span class="process-step__number">01</span><div><h3 class="heading-medium heading-medium--compact"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Set Up Respondents</span></h3><p class="body-copy-small-compact">Provide designated participants with credentials for the TAMS assessment workspace.</p></div></li>
            <li class="trust-card-no-hover process-step-card"><span class="process-step__number">02</span><div><h3 class="heading-medium heading-medium--compact"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Complete the Questionnaire</span></h3><p class="body-copy-small-compact">Capture structured and narrative responses across the six operational domains.</p></div></li>
            <li class="trust-card-no-hover process-step-card"><span class="process-step__number">03</span><div><h3 class="heading-medium heading-medium--compact"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Follow Relevant Paths</span></h3><p class="body-copy-small-compact">Use parent-linked follow-ups to explore the controls, processes, and capabilities that apply.</p></div></li>
            <li class="trust-card-no-hover process-step-card"><span class="process-step__number">04</span><div><h3 class="heading-medium heading-medium--compact"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Generate the Maturity View</span></h3><p class="body-copy-small-compact">Apply Agentic AI scoring to the completed assessment and reveal strengths and areas for improvement.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Outcomes -->
<section class="content-section content-section--light" id="assessment-outcomes">
    <div class="section-container">
        <div class="section-intro">
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent">Clearer Decisions</p>
            <h2 class="section-heading">Turn Assessment Responses into <span>Operational Direction</span></h2>
            <p class="section-intro__description">Give leadership, security, and compliance stakeholders a common evidence base for deciding what to sustain, what to improve, and what to fund next.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-grid">
            <article class="trust-card group"><div class="card-heading-row"><div class="icon-tile icon-tile--primary"><span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-tile__symbol">speed</span></div><h3 class="heading-medium"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Executive Baseline</span></h3></div><p class="body-copy-small">Establish a concise, shared view of current maturity for leadership discussions, governance reviews, and progress tracking.</p></article>
            <article class="trust-card group"><div class="card-heading-row"><div class="icon-tile icon-tile--primary"><span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-tile__symbol">search_insights</span></div><h3 class="heading-medium"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Evidence-Backed Gaps</span></h3></div><p class="body-copy-small">Connect maturity gaps to the ownership, processes, implementation details, and technology described by your respondents.</p></article>
            <article class="trust-card group"><div class="card-heading-row"><div class="icon-tile icon-tile--primary"><span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-tile__symbol">route</span></div><h3 class="heading-medium"><span class="heading-medium__highlight">Prioritized Roadmap</span></h3></div><p class="body-copy-small">Focus investment and improvement work on the areas with the greatest operational relevance instead of treating every gap equally.</p></article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Proven Outcomes -->
<section class="content-section content-section--muted content-section--border-top" id="operational-assessment-results">
    <div class="section-container">
        <div class="proof-card">
            <div class="proof-card__content">
                <div>
                    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent eyebrow--compact">Proven in a Regulated Payment Environment</p>
                    <h2 class="proof-card__heading">One View of <span>Technical and Operational Risk</span></h2>
                    <p class="body-copy-small">For a regulated fintech, Tabiri paired operational assessment with penetration testing so executives, engineers, and compliance stakeholders could act from one body of evidence rather than disconnected questionnaires and scan results.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="proof-card__metrics">
                    <div class="case-metric"><p class="case-metric__value">26</p><p class="body-copy-small-compact">governance domains examined</p></div>
                    <div class="case-metric"><p class="case-metric__value">6</p><p class="body-copy-small-compact">operational security areas connected</p></div>
                    <div class="case-metric"><p class="case-metric__value">PCI DSS</p><p class="body-copy-small-compact">requirements mapped into reporting</p></div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="proof-card__footer">
                <a class="text-link" href="/blog/inside-a-regulated-fintechs-agentic-secops-penetration-test">Read the regulated fintech case study <span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-size-sm">arrow_forward</span></a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- CTA Section -->
<section class="callout-section callout-section--unbordered" id="operational-assessment-cta">
    <div class="callout">
        <div class="callout__overlay"></div>
        <div class="callout__content callout__content--narrow">
            <p class="callout__eyebrow">Know Where You Stand</p>
            <h2 class="callout__heading">Build Your Next <span>Security Decision</span> on a <span>Clear Maturity View</span></h2>
            <p class="callout__description">Bring us the decision, deadline, or compliance pressure behind your assessment. We will help define the right participants and scope for a maturity view your organization can act on.</p>
            <a class="btn-primary" href="/contact">Start the Conversation</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
{{end}}